rite","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","repository_hooks":"write","repository_projects":"write","security_events":"write","statuses":"write","vulnerability_alerts":"read"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6123230527","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/pull/58#issuecomment-6123230527","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/58","id":6123230527,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSN6Nm88AAAABbPkVPw","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-12T11:20:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T11:20:27Z","body":"## AI Security Review\n**Experiment condition:** C\n**Automated operational score:** 70/100 — MEDIUM — APPROVE_WITH_COMMENTS\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **HIGH · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · Inbound HTTP (TCP/80) permitted from any internet source (0.0.0.0/0)**\n  - Category rationale: The Terraform code explicitly configures source_address_prefix = '0.0.0.0/0' with access = 'Allow' on inbound TCP/80, opening the subnet to arbitrary internet sources. This is a concrete, demonstrated security weakness regardless of the deny-all rule at priority 4096, which evaluates after the Allow at priority 302. The tfsec finding AVD-AZU-0047 corroborates this. Policy SEC-001 requires justification and explicit approval for public exposure; the inline comment references TC04 but no supplied policy document or formal exception record authorises this rule for the TC01 research workload.\n  - Evidence: azurerm_network_security_group.nsg, security_rule 'AllowHTTP': priority = 302, direction = 'Inbound', access = 'Allow', protocol = 'Tcp', destination_port_range = '80', source_address_prefix = '0.0.0.0/0'. Associated via azurerm_subnet_network_security_group_association.subnet to azurerm_subnet.subnet (address_prefixes = ['10.0.1.0/24']). tfsec AVD-AZU-0047 independently flags this resource.\n  - Analysis: The NSG security rule 'AllowHTTP' (priority 302, direction Inbound, access Allow, protocol Tcp, destination_port_range 80, source_address_prefix 0.0.0.0/0) allows unrestricted inbound HTTP traffic from any IPv4 address. Because rule priority 302 is evaluated before the DenyAllInbound rule at priority 4096, any host on the internet can reach TCP/80 on resources in the associated subnet. The inline comment states this is 'deliberately public HTTP access for security testing only' referencing TC04, but the supplied policy (SEC-001) requires explicit justification and approval for public exposure, and no such formal approval or exception record is present in the supplied files.\n  - Impact: Any internet host can initiate TCP connections to port 80 on resources within the subnet. If any workload (current or future) listens on TCP/80, it is directly reachable from the public internet with no source restriction. Even in a network-only research context, the rule establishes a permissive baseline that conflicts with the otherwise restrictive deny-all posture and could facilitate reconnaissance or exploitation if a workload is later introduced.\n  - Recommendation: If public HTTP access is genuinely required for the TC04 security testing scenario, restrict source_address_prefix to a specific known IP range or prefix (e.g., a test client CIDR) rather than 0.0.0.0/0, and document the formal approval in policy or as a tagged exception. If this rule is not currently active or needed for TC01, remove the AllowHTTP security_rule block. If the rule must remain, record an explicit SEC-001 exception referencing the approver, scope, and expiry date in a policy register and reference it in the Terraform comment.\n\n### Policy mappings\n- **SEC-001** — No resource should be publicly exposed unless explicitly required and justified. (finding F-001)\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6123230527/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=